/-
Copyright: subproject `OROneRel` -- one-relator combinatorics (node N2).

# The exponent-sum-zero case of the Magnus--Moldavanskii step

`mmStepData_of_expsum_zero` supplies the Magnus--Moldavanskii step `HasMMStepData r` whenever the
cyclically reduced nontrivial relator `r` involves a generator `t` of exponent sum zero in `r`.

The construction is the classical Magnus rewriting.  Writing `r` as a reduced word, delete every
letter `t` and decorate every remaining letter `x` by the exponent sum of `t` in the prefix before
it; a decorated letter `(x,k)` stands for the conjugate `t ^ k * x * t ^ (-k)`.  The resulting word
`w` (over the decorated alphabet `β`) is the Magnus rewriting of `r`: the telescoping identity
`magnusMap t w = r` holds, its length is the number of non-`t` letters of `r`, hence `< relatorNorm
r`, and the rewriting of a cyclically reduced word of exponent sum zero is cyclically reduced.

The decorated alphabet is closed under the shift `(x,k) ↦ (x,k+1)` only along the decorations that
actually occur, so `β` is taken to be the *interval closure* of the occurring decorations.  The
associated subgroups are the Magnus subgroups of `⟨β | w⟩` generated by the decorations
`≤ max - 1`, resp. `≥ min + 1`; the stable letter `t` conjugates the first onto the second and the
defining relations of the HNN extension reproduce the presentation of `⟨α | r⟩` on the generators
`t, y_{x,k}` (`y_{x,k} = t ^ k x t ^ (-k)`) -- the classical Magnus--Moldavanskii step.
-/

